## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> **PyJWT vs python-jose**: I will use PyJWT (simpler, more widely used, no extra dependencies). If you need RS256 asymmetric signing in future, python-jose would be needed — but HS256 is correct for this scope.

> [!NOTE]
> **User store**: The auth system is stateless — it doesn't include a database. `validate_credentials()` takes a stored hash as input (the caller is responsible for looking up the user). This keeps the module educational without pulling in SQLAlchemy.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **`JWT_SECRET_KEY`**: This must be set in `.env` before running. The system will reject secrets shorter than 32 characters and raise `WeakSecretError` at import time.

